{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>לבב</b> — A man whose heart is perverse as well as evil. 'An evil man,' for how can one say that he does not know evil? This is the fool written of them, for they do not know how to do evil — which is innate to man from his youth."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 101, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:39.869004576Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}